From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:32:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] jscript: Intl.Collator, Intl.NumberFormat and
 Intl.DateTimeFormat (IE11 mode)

IE11 has the ECMA-402 1st edition Intl object, built on Windows NLS; Wine's
jscript has none. New intl.c, only created in the ES6 (document mode 11)
language version:

- Intl.Collator: usage, sensitivity (CompareStringEx flags), numeric
  (SORT_DIGITSASNUMBERS), ignorePunctuation, caseFirst; the bound compare
  function; resolvedOptions; supportedLocalesOf.
- Intl.NumberFormat: decimal, percent and currency styles, integer, fraction
  and significant digit options, useGrouping, via GetNumberFormatEx and
  GetCurrencyFormatEx with the locale's grouping, separators and negative
  patterns; the bound format function; resolvedOptions.
- Intl.DateTimeFormat: weekday/era/year/month/day/hour/minute/second/
  timeZoneName/hour12/timeZone ("UTC" only, as IE11), the picture string is
  derived from the locale's date and time patterns and formatted with
  GetDateFormatEx/GetTimeFormatEx.
- Locale tags are validated and canonicalized (RangeError otherwise) and
  resolved with a lookup against the installed locales.
- localeCompare(that, locales, options), Number.prototype.toLocaleString and
  Date.prototype.toLocale(Date|Time)String(locales, options) go through them
  when arguments are given in that mode; the no-argument forms are unchanged.

Tests: new jscript tests/intl.js (run by run.c under the 0x503 language
version) and an mshtml documentmode.js check per document mode.

